(vector (map (:adr/id "adr-2608260800-kotoba-stack-performance-world-class")
  (:adr/title "Kotoba stack performance — measured comparison and world-class gates")
  (:adr/status "accepted")
  (:adr/date "2026-08-26")
  (:adr/doc_type "adr")
  (:adr/source-format "edn")
  (:adr/related (vector "adr-2608262300-kotoba-amu-world-class-proof-scope-and-roadmap"
                 "adr-2608242900-the-oracle-reach-depended-on-module-size"
                 "adr-2607198300-kotoba-native-aot-no-jvm-runtime"
                 "adr-260726-kotobase-query-plane-is-one-ref"))
  (:adr/body "# Kotoba stack performance — measured comparison and world-class gates\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted (2026-08-26). Owner ambition: **#1 in every owned domain**, but only where a versioned benchmark contract and fleet gate say so.\n\n## Context\n\nPrior answers mixed amu (compiler), kototama (tender), aiueos (OS), and legacy Rust kotoba DB numbers. Only **amu** had reproducible cross-engine evidence (`kotoba.runtime-comparison/v1`, `kotoba.performance-baseline/v1` in `orgs/kotoba-lang/amu/docs/performance.md`).\n\n2026-08-26: exploratory run on local M4 (load 17–25). Same day: **official quiet-host run on murakumo judah** (load 1.2–1.4, 7 runs).\n\n## Decision\n\n1. **Superproject evidence plane:** `90-docs/performance/runs/<date>/*.json` + `performance.datoms.edn`; human summaries live in `docs/performance/` (90-docs is EDN-only).\n2. **Weekly snapshot:** update `kotoba-stack-benchmark-<date>.md` or rolling section in roadmap; pin JSON artifacts per date.\n3. **World-class gates** (official quiet-host baseline 2026-08-26 judah):\n   - **amu native narrow kernel:** 6.79 ns vs Rust 6.44 ns = **1.06×** — competitive, not certified #1.\n   - **amu Wasm32:** 6.78× Rust — not #1.\n   - **compile cold:** ~663 ms wasm32 — approaching &lt;500 ms target; semantic edit ~38 ms.\n   - **kototama JVM path:** ~3.4 s per cold fact.wasm (exploratory only) — not #1.\n   - **aiueos:** UNMEASURED — add `kotoba.os-microbench/v1` before any OS perf claim.\n4. **Regression policy:** fleet gate `root-kotoba-stack-performance` verifies pinned judah-quiet JSON + `performance.datoms.edn` agreement on every root merge; `scripts/verify-kotoba-stack-performance.cljs --live` re-runs amu and fails on &gt;5% regression when `orgs/kotoba-lang/amu` is present and load &lt; 4.\n5. **Certification:** use `perfgate.core/qualify` for any \"faster than LLVM/Rust\" claim (see amu `performance.md` kernel_wide section).\n\n## Consequences\n\nPositive: single place to answer \"how fast are we\"; quiet-host numbers on fleet replace laptop-only claims.\nNegative: narrow kernel only; wide kernel and tender/OS still open.\n\n## Evidence paths\n\n- `docs/performance/kotoba-stack-benchmark-2026-08-26.md`\n- `docs/performance/world-class-roadmap.md`\n- `90-docs/performance/performance.datoms.edn`\n- `90-docs/performance/runs/2026-08-26-judah-quiet/runtime.json` (official)\n- `90-docs/performance/runs/2026-08-26-judah-quiet/compile.json` (official)\n- `90-docs/performance/runs/2026-08-26/kotoba-runtime-20260826.json` (exploratory)\n- `scripts/verify-kotoba-stack-performance.cljs`\n- `scripts/fleet-ci/gates/kotoba-stack-performance-check.cljs`\n- amu commit `6889fa736750`\n\n## Resume\n\n2026-08-26: `kotoba.tender-comparison/v1` landed (`scripts/tender-comparison.mjs`, evidence `runs/2026-08-26-tender/`; contended host load ~94). Quiet-host official tender run on judah pending.\n\nNext engineering: roadmap and proof scope — adr-2608262300 (CFG liveness, KIR pipeline, suite). This ADR owns evidence plane and fleet gate only: (1) quiet-host tender re-run, (2) kotoba.os-microbench/v1, (3) optional amu-stack-performance-regression fleet gate on nodes with rustc.")))
